Subject: Preserve copied Wii32 camera event words and compiler fabs type

Upstream-base: 132cdee912111da6c9973b1dce13651f1979b07d

The original thwomp event producer copies one Wii32 word from source offset0;
retail lwz/stw transfers it into the event's second field. The original camera
handler compares that scalar word to3. Its native representation is a u32,
not a host object pointer. Copy only the original four bytes from the already
native source object, retaining source pointers, pool/queue/free operations,
callbacks, field decisions and the entire handler body.

Supply the MWCC __fabs operation with the explicit standard double overload,
retaining the original float subtraction and float result. Keep the original
expression on console; no camera transition, timing or behavior is changed.

Whole source compiler and four-byte host ABI evidence do not establish genuine
camera event dispatch, original camera runtime or complete game startup.

